where p i = π θ ( y i | x ) π θ old ( y i | x ) denotes the probability ratio between the current and old policy, and the normalized advantage is computed as A i = r i -mean ( { r j } G j =1 ) std ( { r j } G j =1 ) , where r i is the reward of the i -th response. The KL divergence term D KL penalizes deviation from a reference policy π θ ref to stabilize training. Here, ϵ is the clipping threshold, and β controls the strength of the KL penalty.

